            <ArticleTitle>Criteria for the safe discharge of patients from the recovery room.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Guidelines need to be in place to help nurses in the recovery room make appropriate and safe decisions when discharging patients to a surgical ward. Consciousness level, respiration, circulation, pain control, homeostasis and wound care should all be considered. Criteria from the Freeman Hospital provides practical guidance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
